  "notes": "{駆|か}けつける is an intransitive ichidan verb. A compound of {駆|か}ける (to run/dash) and つける (to arrive at).\n\nASPECT (ている):\nRarely used in the ている form. The focus is on the act of rushing to a place.\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- [place]に{駆|か}けつける — to rush to [place]\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {現場|げんば}に{駆|か}けつける (rush to the scene)\n- {病院|びょういん}に{駆|か}けつける (rush to the hospital)\n- {応援|おうえん}に{駆|か}けつける (rush to give support)\n\nImplies urgency and physical movement. Often used when someone responds quickly to an emergency or important event.",
